text:
alex: Quick check — we're planning to stop accepting the old v1 payload shape (the nested `request.body.payload` envelope) on 2024-08-15. Proposal: roll a short-lived "payload-gate" sanitizer as a thin shim in front of the API to translate v1 -> v2 for a 90d grace period. It lives in the edge tier, feature-flagged per-tenant. Thoughts?
maria: How much latency are we talking for the sanitizer? even a few ms at p95 could matter for realtime customers. :eyes:
alex: Measured on a small prototype: median + ~2.8ms, p95 + ~9–12ms when CPU-backed and under light load. If we place it on the same fast path as existing routing (no extra RPC) it's lower; if it calls out to KV for lookup it's worse. We can keep it pure transform + heuristics to avoid KV.
sam: Important: caching keys change if we rewrite payload shapes. If we translate v1->v2 we must normalize the cache key (e.g., canonicalize prompt + model + truncation flags) otherwise we break hit rates and double write. Also session KV (kv-cache for prefix tokens) has different keys per shape — need a migration or namespace alias.
leah: Agreed. Also: add `X-Deprecation-Notice: v1-retire-2024-08-15` in the response headers for translated requests so SDKs can log and customers can see the warning. We'll include docs + a prominent notice in Console.
alex: Plan sketch: (1) deploy payload-gate behind a tenant opt-in flag; (2) canary at 1% for 24h -> 10% for 48h -> ramp 90% -> full for opt-ins; (3) run it in passthrough mode for others (no translation); (4) after 30d send deprecation header to opt-ins and non-opt-ins; (5) stop auto-translate after 90d for tenants that haven't migrated. Rollback: feature-flag off.
ci-bot: deploy: payload-gate v0.1 scheduled to staging at 1719906000 — tests: routing, latency, cache-key-preserve.
maria: SDKs: we should ship a minor bump that warns on v1 usage and offers an automated client migration helper. Grace period for SDK users? 30 days after the header start felt tight for some customers.
alex: Proposal: 30d for explicit SDK warnings + 60d server auto-translate for opt-ins; full removal at 90d. That gives ops time to monitor and customers time to upgrade. We'll also publish an incremental migration guide.
sam: Logging: add a sampled raw-payload dump (opt-in via tenant flag) with scrubbing (PII redaction) for failures so we can debug translation mismatches. We'll keep sampling at 0.1% by default.
leah: Error handling: which classes do we auto-fix vs surface as 4xx? My vote: whitespace/quote-style, deprecated field names -> auto-fix; structural mismatches (missing required field) -> 400 with a clear migration hint. Also add a `X-Compat-Translated: true|false` header so customers can correlate.
alex: Agreed. Example nginx-ish rule for the thin shim (very rough):
```
location /v2/api {
  if ($http_x_api_version = "1") {
    proxy_set_header X-Compat-Translated true;
    rewrite_by_lua_block {
      -- parse body, canonicalize envelope, map to v2 fields
    }
  }
  proxy_pass http://service-upstream;
}
```
maria: Love it. I'll start the SDK deprecation PR and update quickstart snippets. I'll own docs and the Console banner. :thumbsup:
leah: I'll add observability TODOs: meter for translated_count, translation_error_ratio, p50/p95 delta, cache_hit_rate delta. We'll want alerting if translation_error_ratio > 1% or p95 delta > 25ms.
alex: I'll file a short RFC with the rollout timeline and link to this thread. Thanks everyone — let's sync tomorrow after the staging run. :coffee:
